    "reason": "The agent demonstrably executed an LSTM 21-day-to-7-day forecasting workflow and reported a test RMSE. Its RMSE differs from the reference, but the discrepancy is reasonably explained by a valid alternative time-series implementation: the agent first applies a chronological 80/20 raw-series split, fits scaling on training values only, and constructs windows separately inside each partition; the reference scales the complete series before making all windows and then splits the windows. The agent's approach avoids both future-informed scaling and train/test-boundary window overlap, so the different test set and resulting RMSE do not establish an error. Although the CSV includes additional MAE and MAPE rows and calls the metric 'RMSE' rather than 'Test_RMSE,' execution logs explicitly identify it as the Test RMSE, and the required Metric/Value columns are present.",
    "reference_method": "The reference MinMax-scales the entire ICU occupancy series, forms all overlapping 21-input/7-output windows, chronologically divides those windows 80/20, trains a two-layer LSTM with an internal validation split, inverse-transforms predictions, and computes flattened test-window RMSE.",
